---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import victor from "../assets/victor.png";
import consuelo from "../assets/victor-consuelo.jpeg";
---

<Page
	title="About · Víctor Kuminov"
	description="Hi, I'm Víctor. 20 years in digital, a two-senior studio with Nina, and a story that ties me to Asturias in northern Spain."
>
	<section class="hero hero--page">
		<div class="container about-hero">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
				<h1>Hi, I'm Víctor</h1>
				<p class="lead">
					I got into this almost by accident. I was looking for someone to build a website the way I
					imagined it, and nobody got it right. So I built it myself. My friends saw it, asked for
					theirs, and that was more than 20 years ago.
				</p>
				<p>
					Since school I've been passionate about advertising: while others went out partying, I went
					to trade fairs and to the big agencies' award shows, BBDO and Leo Burnett. That mix of
					creativity and business is still how I work.
				</p>
			</div>
			<figure>
				<Image src={victor} alt="Víctor Kuminov" widths={[360, 520, 720]} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 420px, 90vw" loading="eager" class="portrait" />
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section--alt">
		<div class="container split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">The studio</p>
				<h2>Two seniors, zero middlemen</h2>
			</div>
			<div>
				<p class="lead">
					Behind every project are <strong>Nina and me</strong>. Nina, my wife, is an exceptional
					developer: she was one of the first developers at one of the major e-commerce platforms, and
					she sees whole systems, where they fail and how to fix them.
				</p>
				<h3>Why a two-person studio and not an agency?</h3>
				<p>
					Because at an agency your project goes through a salesperson, an account manager and a
					junior learning on your money. Here you talk to the person who designs and the person who
					builds. Every project carries my name, and that's the best guarantee it will come out
					flawless.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">How I work</p>
				<h2>I tell you the truth, even when it doesn't suit me</h2>
			</div>
			<div>
				<p class="lead">
					I'll tell you where you're overspending, what won't work in your case, and when it's worth
					investing and when it isn't.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>I work for my reputation, not to bill more.</strong> If you're not satisfied, I redo
					it or give you your money back.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section--alt">
		<div class="container split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Experience</p>
				<h2>20 years, 100+ projects</h2>
			</div>
			<div>
				<ul class="checks">
					<li>20 years in digital and more than 100 projects.</li>
					<li>International brands such as <strong>LG</strong>, <strong>Sisley</strong> and <strong>Toyota</strong>.</li>
					<li><strong>Platinum partner</strong> of a leading e-commerce platform.</li>
					<li>An in-house online store platform, with its own admin panel, chat sales and an AI assistant.</li>
					<li>A client who has been with me for more than 10 years.</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="muted" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
					Languages: I work in English, Spanish and Russian, in writing, and in German through my
					team. Fully remote, with clients across Spain, Europe and beyond.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="narrow prose">
			<p class="eyebrow">My story</p>
			<h2 style="margin-top:0">What ties me to Asturias</h2>
			<p>
				My grandmother's best friend was one of the Asturian children the Spanish Civil War sent far
				from home, all the way to Russia. She was fond of him all her life. And, leaving politics
				aside, life brought me, her grandson, to Asturias. Like a circle closing.
			</p>
			<p>
				I arrived almost by chance. I lived in Barcelona for six months and never quite felt at home:
				too hot, too crowded, too little nature. At the hotel someone told me about Asturias, and I came
				to see it. I got off the plane, took the bus, saw the landscape and fell in love at first
				sight. The next day I was already looking for a flat so I could stay. I found one I liked and
				bought it that same day, without looking at any other.
			</p>
			<p>
				Asturias gives me back something of my childhood: the smells, the views, the calm. Not long
				ago I met <strong>Consuelo Argüelles</strong>, author of <em>"Mi odisea en la URSS"</em>, one
				of those war children. The story my grandmother used to tell me suddenly had a face and a name.
			</p>
			<figure style="margin:2.5rem 0">
				<Image src={consuelo} alt="Víctor with Consuelo Argüelles, author of Mi odisea en la URSS" widths={[400, 680]} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 680px, 92vw" class="portrait" />
				<figcaption>With Consuelo Argüelles, author of "Mi odisea en la URSS".</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<h3>My mission</h3>
			<p>
				What I did for that craft manufacturer, I want to do here: take what Asturias does so well to
				the whole world, and show the world this land and its people.
				<a href="/sell-worldwide">Here's how</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<CtaBand title="Shall we talk?" />
</Page>

<style>
	.about-hero {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--s5);
		align-items: center;
	}
	@media (min-width: 900px) {
		.about-hero {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 400px;
			gap: var(--s6);
		}
	}
	.about-hero .portrait {
		aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
		max-width: 400px;
	}
	@media (max-width: 899px) {
		.about-hero .portrait {
			max-width: 280px;
		}
	}
</style>
